 Normal functions : function name(parameters){code}

Arrow functions : const name=(parameters)=>{code}


1. This binding -
 Normal functions make their own this context.
 Arrow functions do not have their own this context. Instead, they inherit
 this from the surrounding non-arrow function or global context.
 bind,call,apply keywords bind the this context of functions but they DO NOT WORK with arrow functions.
 Arrow function cannot be used as object methods and constructors because of this reason.


2. Return
 Normal functions need to have explicit return keyword to return any value/values.
 Arrow functions have implicit return -
 ()=>code this is implicit return
 ()=>{return code} here return keyword needs to be used for returning values
 ()=>({}) this is how a object returned from arrow functions.

3.arguments and yield:
 3.1 Arrow functions do not have access to arguments object, which normal functions have,
     reasong being same that they are light weight and do not bind their arguments and inherit
     if from outer scope.
 3.2 Arrow functions call also not be used as generator functions cause they cannot use yield
     inside their body, they do not have their own context which are mandatory for working of
     generator functions.
4. Prototype
   Arrow functions do not have prototype property and do not implement [[construct]] internal
   method which are mandatory for function to act as constructor and thus now work with new keyword.

5. JS just like java is strictly pass by value.
  - which means primitives get their values copied when passed.
  - and non primitives the value of reference in copied when passed.

